# Fifth input graph — the exact decoder bug the upstream test guards
# against: the empty legacy Text.value leaks as an EMPTY literal
# (`ontouml:value ""`). `any(g.triples(...))` yields a (s, p, o) tuple,
# truthy whatever the literal, and `bool(m{ ... [] })` counts solutions:
# both must report the third assertion failing, an empty literal being
# present, not absent.
@prefix ex:       <https://example.org#> .
@prefix ontouml:  <https://w3id.org/ontouml#> .
@prefix rdf:      <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

ex:view-1_shape rdf:type ontouml:Text ;
    ontouml:value "" .
